  "exclusions": [
    "Trust-boundary cases are excluded from TP/TN/FP/FN and pixel-quality denominators and are reported separately.",
    "Calibration and development cases are excluded from release-gate point estimates, except split, trust, repeatability, and regression gates that explicitly name broader scope.",
    "LOW severity is excluded from the primary recall gate but remains in all reports and the positive-case Dice gate.",
    "A case with missing or invalid authoritative truth invalidates the run; it is not silently excluded.",
    "Cases outside the frozen manifest are not added after test results are observed.",
    "The gray transition intervals between supported and abstain nuisance ranges are not generated in E1 v1.",
    "MVTec, real workshop images, private data, and downloaded third-party image bytes are not E1 inputs.",
    "Hardlink behavior is a supplemental platform-specific security test and is not one of the portable 24 trust cases.",
    "Human-disposition binding uses explicitly synthetic test fixtures only and must not be described as completed human UAT.",
    "A failed or abstained case remains in its applicable denominator unless the metric definition explicitly separates trust cases."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "E1 is deterministic synthetic evidence and does not estimate shop-floor accuracy.",
    "One synthetic part family, two revisions, and three rendered views do not represent industrial diversity.",
    "The image-difference baseline remains sensitive to unmodeled lighting, optics, material, pose, focus, and background changes.",
    "Synthetic masks are exact generator truth and may make localization easier than human-labeled real defects.",
    "The threshold 0.0025 predates E1 and is not covered by the baseline configuration SHA-256; the E1 protocol digest binds it separately.",
    "The calibration split may only confirm the single preregistered threshold; a failure requires a new protocol version.",
    "LOW-severity recall is exploratory and is not a release gate, but it cannot be hidden.",
    "A hash proves byte identity, not capture authenticity, manufacturing conformance, or lawful provenance.",
    "Bundle integrity and fail-closed tests do not establish security or safety certification.",
    "DEMO_READY_E1 does not mean FIELD_READY, production release authority, shipment approval, or inspector replacement."
  ]
